\section{Centered CKA Heatmaps}
\label{sec:cka_heatmap}

\begin{figure}[t]
\centering
\includegraphics[width=\columnwidth]{figures/cka_heatmap.pdf}
\caption{Centered CKA similarity~\citep{kornblith2019cka} between encoder variants on IID and OOD data for DeBERTa-v3 and RoBERTa. Low off-diagonal values (vanilla vs.\ adapted variants) confirm that continued pretraining substantially reshapes representations; the MLM vs.\ 9-class block shows distinct geometries (CKA $\leq$ 0.2 on RoBERTa OOD).}
\label{fig:cka_heatmap}
\end{figure}

\section{Reproducibility Details}
\label{sec:reproducibility}

\paragraph{Stage-1 training.}
All variants use DeBERTa-v3-base (184M parameters) with learning rate $2 \times 10^{-5}$, AdamW optimizer ($\beta_1$=0.9, $\beta_2$=0.999, weight decay 0.01), linear warmup over the first 10\% of steps, batch size 16, and 4 epochs. MLM variants use 15\% random token masking. Training takes approximately 30 minutes per variant on a single NVIDIA A100 (40GB).

\paragraph{Stage-2 training.}
The BiGRU has hidden dimension 128 (bidirectional, so output dimension 256). The MLP classifier has layers $256 \to 64 \to 2$ with ReLU activation and dropout 0.3. Training uses learning rate $1 \times 10^{-3}$, Adam optimizer, batch size 32, and 20 epochs with early stopping (patience 5) on validation F1. Stage-2 training completes in under 5 minutes per variant.

\paragraph{Data generation.}
Jailbreak conversations are generated using Qwen3-8B with attack-specific prompt templates. Crescendo conversations follow a 5--8 turn gradual escalation structure. FITD conversations use a 2--3 turn commitment-consistency structure. Deceptive Delight conversations embed harmful content within emotionally engaging 3--5 turn sequences. Benign conversations are generated with topic-anchored prompts across five domains (technology, health, finance, education, general) with matched turn counts.

\paragraph{Strategy annotation.}
Each user turn is annotated by Qwen3-8B using a structured prompt that provides definitions and two examples for each of the nine strategy categories. The prompt instructs the model to output a single category label. We plan to release all generation and annotation prompts, the full dataset, and training code upon acceptance.

\paragraph{Adversarial paraphrasing.}
The paraphrased test set is generated by instructing Qwen3-8B to rephrase each user turn while preserving the communicative intent. The resulting paraphrases have mean BERTScore 0.92 and mean lexical overlap 0.20 with the originals. These metrics confirm substantial surface-level variation.

\paragraph{Domain exposure is the primary mechanism.}
MLM bridges $\sim$60\,pp from vanilla (0.312$\pm$0.026 $\to$ 0.914$\pm$0.115) without labels, confirming the DAPT interpretation~\citep{gururangan2020dontstop}. TF-IDF collapse on ActorAttack (0.261 vs.\ 9-class 0.972) confirms that domain-adapted representations capture features beyond lexical overlap.
All three classification-supervised variants converge to equivalent detection (F1 = 0.997--1.000); McNemar's test finds no significant pairwise differences (all $p > 0.13$; $\leq$7 discordant pairs limit power), and paired permutation tests confirm equivalence ($p \geq 0.40$). TOST equivalence tests (margin = 5\,pp) confirm statistical equivalence on DD (all $p < 0.01$, 90\% CI within $\pm$0.05). On ActorAttack, equivalence cannot be statistically confirmed due to limited seeds ($n$=3), though observed mean differences (2--4\,pp) fall within practical equivalence margins. Label quality and granularity are non-factors for detection.
Classification supervision reduces cross-seed variance 4--20$\times$ over MLM on synthetic OOD (std 0.005 vs.\ 0.115 on DD; bootstrap CI widths: 5.7\,pp vs.\ 35.5\,pp). This stability benefit does not transfer to human-authored data, where classification-supervised variants exhibit the highest variance and pure MLM the lowest (Section~\ref{sec:human_data}).

\paragraph{Domain specificity is marginal at full length but meaningful for early detection.}
Wikipedia MLM (0.904$\pm$0.115) nearly matches jailbreak-domain MLM at full length (1\,pp gap); general continued pretraining provides most of the representational benefit.

